          "LS": 54.8,
          "ES": 93.5
        },
        "DiffusionDrive": {
          "DS": 34.2,
          "RC": 58.3,
          "LS": 49.1,
          "ES": 91.4
        },
        "SimLingo": {
          "DS": 42.3,
          "RC": 70.5,
          "LS": 63.3,
          "ES": 94.8
        },
        "KnowVal": {
          "DS": 46.6,
          "RC": 73.8,
          "LS": 69.3,
          "ES": 97.4
        }
      },
      "caveats": [
        "Report RC/LS/ES separately; DS is a product.",
        "Repository says academic research only unless commercial permission is obtained.",
        "EthicsScore is benchmark-defined, not universal ethical truth.",
        "Do not multiply the published aggregate RC, LS and ES columns to reconstruct aggregate DS; DS is averaged after per-route multiplication and ES has a subset denominator.",
        "The paper's table includes nine baselines: TCP, UniAD-Base, VAD, ThinkTwice, DriveAdapter, DriveTransformer, ORION, DiffusionDrive, SimLingo and KnowVal."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09972",
        "https://github.com/VDIGPKU/HiDrive"
      ],
      "aggregation": {
        "per_route_formula": "DS_i = RC_i * LS_i * ES_i",
        "split_level": {
          "DS": "mean(DS_i) over all valid routes",
          "RC": "mean(RC_i) over all valid routes",
          "LS": "mean(LS_i) over all valid routes",
          "ES": "mean(ES_i) over ethics-applicable routes only"
        },
        "implication": "Aggregate DS is not generally equal to aggregate RC * aggregate LS * aggregate ES because the product is taken per route before averaging, and ES can use a different denominator."
      },
      "metric_semantics": [
        "RC is usually passed-waypoints / total-waypoints, but selected dilemma scenarios may set RC=1 after their safety-critical primary objective is completed.",
        "LS is affected by legal events, collisions and route-lane events; it is not a pure traffic-law-only score.",
        "Brake-aware relief changes selected collision penalty coefficients when braking occurred within the declared two-frame window.",
        "ES includes social/normative events and its split-level mean is computed only over ethics-applicable routes."
      ]
    },
